.TH feupdateenv 3 "2026-05-03" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
feupdateenv \- restore environment and re-raise saved exceptions
.SH LIBRARY
Math Library (libm, \-lm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fenv.h>
.PP
.B "int feupdateenv( " const fenv_t * envp " );"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBfeupdateenv()\fR function updates the current floating-point
environment using the object pointed to by
.BR envp .
This object must have been saved by a previous call to
\fBfeholdexcept()\fR.

The function:
.TP
1. Saves any currently set exception flags.
.TP
2. Restores the rounding mode and exception state from
   .B envp.
.TP
3. Or\-s the saved exception flags back (re\-raising them).

This allows exception flags that were set during the computation to be
preserved and raised after restoring the original rounding mode and
environment. It avoids losing exception information that was raised after
\fBfeholdexcept()\fR cleared them.

On x86, this corresponds to saving MXCSR/x87 status flags, restoring the
x87 control word or MXCSR from the saved state, and then re-ORing the
previously captured flags.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The \fBfeupdateenv()\fR function returns zero on success.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
The environment object was not saved by a previous
\fBfeholdexcept()\fR call, or is otherwise invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
#include <fenv.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <math.h>

double safe_sqrt(double x) {
    fenv_t saved_env;

    /* Save env, clear flags, set default rounding */
    feholdexcept(&saved_env);

    double result = sqrt(x);
    /* Any exceptions raised during sqrt() are captured */

    /* Restore saved rounding mode and re-raise any new exceptions */
    feupdateenv(&saved_env);

    return result;
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfenv\fR(7), \fBfeholdexcept\fR(3), \fBfegetenv\fR(3), \fBfetestexcept\fR(3)
